1
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:19,080
Hi everyone, welcome back to our listening course.

2
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,820
In this lesson, we're going to practice two

3
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:24,380
more question types in IELTS Listening Tests.

4
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,940
Table Completion and Summary Completion.

5
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,000
And the steps to do these types are

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,800
quite similar to those of Sentence Completion and

7
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
Short Answer Questions.

8
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,240
The challenging thing is how we avoid all

9
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,980
the distractors and increase the percentage of correct

10
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,040
answers to 100%.

11
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:45,940
In this lesson, we are going to review

12
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:48,920
the format and key features of Table Completion

13
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:52,460
and Summary Completion question types in the IELTS

14
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:53,260
Listening Test.

15
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,860
Understand and apply effective steps to answer Table

16
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:00,320
and Summary Completion questions by understanding the topic,

17
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:05,860
underlining keywords and predicting paraphrases before listening.

18
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,200
And finally, apply tips to watch for distractors

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,500
and carefully check your answers in practice exercises.

20
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:15,980
By the end of this lesson, you'll feel

21
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:19,040
more confident to tackle Table and Summary Completion

22
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,360
questions in the IELTS Listening Test.

23
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,220
So let's get started.

24
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:28,800
Table Completion in IELTS Listening requires candidates to

25
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,600
listen and fill in the blanks to complete

26
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,680
a table of information.

27
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,640
Typically, the table will have column headings or

28
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,380
row headings to help you easily identify which

29
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:40,520
information to look for.

30
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:43,460
In this question type, you will often hear

31
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,620
information in the table row by row from

32
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:49,440
top to bottom or from left to right.

33
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,300
This question type is commonly found in Section

34
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:55,100
1 and Section 2 of the IELTS Listening

35
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:55,520
Test.

36
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,360
This is an example of Table Completion.

37
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:05,100
Summary Completion requires you to fill in the

38
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,120
blanks to complete a given summary.

39
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,360
This question type can be found in all

40
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,620
parts of the IELTS Listening Test, but most

41
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,120
frequently in Section 3 and Section 4.

42
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:17,700
And here is an example of Summary Completion.

43
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,640
Here are the steps for Table Completion and

44
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,600
Summary Completion.

45
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,040
Step 1.

46
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,560
You have to read the requirement to identify

47
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,240
the word limit.

48
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,780
Some common requirements include Write one word only

49
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:33,880
for each answer.

50
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,660
Write no more than two words for each

51
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:38,060
answer.

52
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:41,480
Write no more than two words and or

53
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,020
a number for each answer.

54
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:47,520
Write no more than three words for each

55
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:47,900
answer.

56
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,120
Write no more than three words and or

57
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,820
a number for each answer.

58
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,580
Step 2.

59
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,900
You have to read the title to understand

60
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,120
the topic of the listening.

61
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:02,640
It shows the topic being discussed and helps

62
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,960
you understand the content of the recording better.

63
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,860
Since then, it helps you know when the

64
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,780
speaker comes to the part that contains the

65
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:10,580
correct answers.

66
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:12,540
Step 3.

67
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:16,480
You have to read questions, underline keywords, predict

68
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,160
paraphrases of the keywords and what type of

69
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,880
information is missing from each blank.

70
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:23,980
The words must be directly taken from the

71
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:26,860
recording and most of the time you won't

72
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,560
need to change their part of speech.

73
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,640
Another thing is that you should pay attention

74
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,820
to distractors.

75
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,680
The distractors in these question types lie in

76
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,960
the way the speaker talks.

77
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:40,620
Distractors often contain the information that is closely

78
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,760
related to the answers.

79
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:45,000
However, it will be modified or corrected through

80
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,480
the use of signal words.

81
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:50,440
However, but, apart from and except.

82
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,540
In step 4, when listening, you will move

83
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,720
your mouse cursor or pen to the keywords

84
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,960
and write the answers.

85
00:03:58,780 --> 00:03:59,440
Step 5.

86
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:04,180
Check answers, spelling, grammatical mistakes, meanings of the words.

87
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,720
After you listen, don't forget to check your answers.

88
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,320
You need to check the spelling, grammatical structures

89
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,800
and meanings of the words you filled in

90
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:16,000
to see if they are suitable for the

91
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:16,459
blanks.

